WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:01.560
- [Instructor] Let's talk a little bit

00:01.560 --> 00:03.323
about congruence, congruence.

00:04.940 --> 00:07.040
And one way to think about congruence,

00:07.040 --> 00:09.550
it's really kind of
equivalence for shapes.

00:09.550 --> 00:11.010
So when, in algebra, when something

00:11.010 --> 00:12.150
is equal to another thing,

00:12.150 --> 00:13.970
it means that their
quantities are the same.

00:13.970 --> 00:16.100
But, if we're now all of a
sudden talking about shapes,

00:16.100 --> 00:18.900
and we say that those shapes are the same,

00:18.900 --> 00:22.890
the shapes are the same size and shape,

00:22.890 --> 00:24.330
then we say that they're congruent.

00:24.330 --> 00:26.880
And just to see a simple example here,

00:26.880 --> 00:30.050
I have this triangle right over there,

00:30.050 --> 00:32.783
and let's say I have this
triangle right over here.

00:33.690 --> 00:37.060
And, if you are able to
shift, if you are able

00:37.060 --> 00:39.980
to shift this triangle
and rotate this triangle

00:39.980 --> 00:42.650
and flip this triangle, you
can make it look exactly

00:42.650 --> 00:45.030
like this triangle, as
long as you're not changing

00:45.030 --> 00:47.290
the lengths of any of the
sides or the angles here.

00:47.290 --> 00:51.470
But you can flip it, you
can shift it and rotate it.

00:51.470 --> 00:54.600
So you can shift, let me
write this, you can shift it,

00:54.600 --> 00:58.450
you can flip it, you can
flip it and you can rotate.

00:58.450 --> 01:00.500
If you can do those three procedures

01:00.500 --> 01:02.790
to make the exact same
triangle and make them

01:02.790 --> 01:06.050
look exactly the same,
then they are congruent.

01:06.050 --> 01:08.300
And, if you say that a
triangle is congruent,

01:08.300 --> 01:09.210
and let me label these.

01:09.210 --> 01:14.150
So let's call this triangle A, B and C.

01:14.150 --> 01:17.860
And let's call this D, oh
let me call it X, Y and Z,

01:17.860 --> 01:22.070
X, Y and Z.

01:22.070 --> 01:24.410
So, if we were to say,
if we make the claim

01:24.410 --> 01:26.460
that both of these
triangles are congruent,

01:26.460 --> 01:30.827
so, if we say triangle ABC is congruent,

01:30.827 --> 01:32.100
and the way you specify it,

01:32.100 --> 01:33.530
it looks almost like an equal sign,

01:33.530 --> 01:36.170
but it's an equal sign with
this little curly thing on top.

01:36.170 --> 01:37.590
Let me write it a little bit neater.

01:37.590 --> 01:39.650
So we would write it like this.

01:39.650 --> 01:42.630
If we know that triangle ABC is congruent

01:42.630 --> 01:45.833
to triangle XY, XYZ,

01:47.963 --> 01:50.730
that means that their corresponding sides

01:50.730 --> 01:51.700
have the same length,

01:51.700 --> 01:53.810
and their corresponding angles,

01:53.810 --> 01:56.710
and their corresponding
angles have the same measure.

01:56.710 --> 01:59.970
So, if we make this assumption,
or if someone tells us

01:59.970 --> 02:04.230
that this is true, then we
know, then we know, for example,

02:04.230 --> 02:08.500
that AB is going to be equal
to XY, the length of segment AB

02:08.500 --> 02:12.060
is going to be equal to
the length of segment XY.

02:12.060 --> 02:14.070
And we could denote it like this.

02:14.070 --> 02:17.110
And I'm assuming that these
are the corresponding sides.

02:17.110 --> 02:19.505
And you can see it actually by the way

02:19.505 --> 02:20.860
we've defined these triangles.

02:20.860 --> 02:24.580
A corresponds to X, B corresponds to Y,

02:24.580 --> 02:27.390
and then C corresponds
to Z right over there.

02:27.390 --> 02:32.130
So AB, side AB, is going to
have the same length as side XY,

02:32.130 --> 02:33.790
and you can sometimes, if
you don't have the colors,

02:33.790 --> 02:35.490
you would denote it just like that.

02:35.490 --> 02:39.670
These, these two lengths,
or these two line segments,

02:39.670 --> 02:40.700
have the same length.

02:40.700 --> 02:43.320
And you can actually say
this, and you don't always

02:43.320 --> 02:47.290
see it written this way, you
could also make the statement

02:47.290 --> 02:50.310
that line segment AB is congruent,

02:50.310 --> 02:54.040
is congruent to line segment XY.

02:54.040 --> 02:57.870
But congruence of line
segments really just means

02:57.870 --> 02:59.590
that their lengths are equivalent.

02:59.590 --> 03:02.010
So these two things mean the same thing.

03:02.010 --> 03:04.470
If one line segment is congruent
to another line segment,

03:04.470 --> 03:06.410
that just means the
measure of one line segment

03:06.410 --> 03:08.820
is equal to the measure
of the other line segment.

03:08.820 --> 03:11.310
And so, we can go through
all the corresponding sides.

03:11.310 --> 03:14.750
If these two characters are
congruent, we also know,

03:14.750 --> 03:19.560
we also know that BC, we
also know the length of BC

03:19.560 --> 03:23.150
is going to be the length of YZ,

03:23.150 --> 03:25.860
assuming that those are
the corresponding sides.

03:25.860 --> 03:28.080
And we could put these double
hash marks right over here

03:28.080 --> 03:31.470
to show that this one, that
these two lengths are the same.

03:31.470 --> 03:34.120
And then, if we go to the third side,

03:34.120 --> 03:37.290
we also know that these are
going to have the same length,

03:37.290 --> 03:40.710
or the line segments themselves
are going to be congruent.

03:40.710 --> 03:44.270
So we also know that the
length of AC, the length of AC

03:44.270 --> 03:47.910
is going to be equal to the length of XZ,

03:47.910 --> 03:50.820
is going to be equal to the length of XZ.

03:50.820 --> 03:53.700
Not only do we know that all
of the corresponding sides

03:53.700 --> 03:54.830
are going to have the same length,

03:54.830 --> 03:56.910
if someone tells us that
a triangle is congruent,

03:56.910 --> 03:59.160
we also know that all
the corresponding angles

03:59.160 --> 04:01.010
are going to have the same measure.

04:01.010 --> 04:04.380
So, for example, we
also know, we also know

04:04.380 --> 04:08.030
that this angle's measure
is going to be the same

04:08.030 --> 04:09.710
as the corresponding angle's measure,

04:09.710 --> 04:12.110
and the corresponding
angle is right over here.

04:12.110 --> 04:14.350
It's between this orange
side and this blue side,

04:14.350 --> 04:16.860
or this orange side and this
purple side, I should say,

04:16.860 --> 04:19.220
in between the orange
side and this purple side.

04:19.220 --> 04:23.270
And so, it also tells us
that the measure, the measure

04:23.270 --> 04:27.710
of angle, what's this,
BAC, measure of angle BAC,

04:27.710 --> 04:32.207
is equal to the measure
of angle, of angle YXZ,

04:33.177 --> 04:35.620
the measure of angle, let
me write that angle symbol

04:35.620 --> 04:39.470
a little less like a,
measure of angle YXZ, YXZ.

04:41.630 --> 04:44.213
We can also write that as angle BAC

04:45.980 --> 04:49.123
is congruent to angle YXZ.

04:50.070 --> 04:52.060
And, once again, like line segments,

04:52.060 --> 04:55.250
if one line segment is congruent
to another line segment,

04:55.250 --> 04:57.220
it just means that
their lengths are equal.

04:57.220 --> 05:00.010
And, if one angle is
congruent to another angle,

05:00.010 --> 05:02.860
it just means that their
measures are equal.

05:02.860 --> 05:04.780
So we know that those
two corresponding angles

05:04.780 --> 05:06.970
have the same measure, they're congruent.

05:06.970 --> 05:09.140
We also know that these
two corresponding angles

05:09.140 --> 05:10.000
have the same measure.

05:10.000 --> 05:12.330
I'll use a double arc to specify that this

05:12.330 --> 05:13.730
has the same measure as that.

05:13.730 --> 05:18.730
So we also know that the measure,
the measure of angle ABC,

05:20.510 --> 05:25.510
ABC, is equal to the
measure of angle XYZ, XYZ.

05:27.840 --> 05:31.720
And then, finally, we know, we finally,

05:31.720 --> 05:33.840
we know that this angle,

05:33.840 --> 05:36.360
if we know that these two
characters are congruent,

05:36.360 --> 05:38.110
that this angle's going
to have the same measure

05:38.110 --> 05:40.030
as this angle, as its corresponding angle.

05:40.030 --> 05:44.810
So we know that the
measure of angle ACB, ACB,

05:46.360 --> 05:50.393
is going to be equal to the
measure of angle XZY, XZY.

05:53.230 --> 05:55.300
Now, what we're gonna
concern ourselves a lot with

05:55.300 --> 05:57.440
is how do we prove
congruence 'cause it's cool.

05:57.440 --> 05:59.860
'Cause if you can prove
congruence of two triangles,

05:59.860 --> 06:02.810
then all of a sudden you can
make all of these assumptions.
